`
` Holder-backed declarations (kind StyleValueKind.object) keep their descriptor or boxed wide value
` GC-reachable through held. During a dynamic replacement, settled-held temporarily keeps the
` holder named by the still-published computed bits alive until settling replaces those bits.
` held-shift and held-tag compose the stable handle into the slot bits: plain descriptors store the
` handle directly (shift 0, tag 0), union cases shift it over the authored case tag.

